00:21:35,101 --> 00:21:41,100
But the bridge that lay just beyond the arts sorely lacked the grace of its entrance.

280
00:21:41,101 --> 00:21:47,100
When they created the Manhattan Bridge, which in scale and in usage is completely 20th century,

281
00:21:47,101 --> 00:21:53,100
the Manhattan Bridge was a heavy-duty urban bridge with a vehicle roadway,

282
00:21:53,101 --> 00:21:59,100
space for subways and L trains, trolleys, and of course a pedestrian walkway.

283
00:21:59,101 --> 00:22:05,100
At the Manhattan end and at the Brooklyn end, they wanted great triumphal arches,

284
00:22:05,101 --> 00:22:09,100
and they hired Carrier and Hastings, who did the public library on 42nd Street.

285
00:22:09,101 --> 00:22:17,100
If you were to compare, say, the towers, the stone towers of the Brooklyn Bridge, which was opened in 1883,

286
00:22:17,101 --> 00:22:23,100
to the steel towers of the Manhattan Bridge, which was opened in 1909,

287
00:22:23,101 --> 00:22:26,100
you'll both notice that they are in a neo-Gothic style.

