00:23:20,141 --> 00:23:24,460
hanging the suspender ropes and then they would put the stringers across and they would

299
00:23:24,461 --> 00:23:29,460
start next to the towers and then start building out wood on both sides.

300
00:23:29,461 --> 00:23:32,700
So then in a sense the bridge grew from the outside in.

301
00:23:32,701 --> 00:23:34,060
It was hard labor.

302
00:23:34,061 --> 00:23:37,020
It was very long days.

303
00:23:37,021 --> 00:23:42,300
They didn't have the ability to have mechanized equipment move heavy blocks and so a lot of

304
00:23:42,301 --> 00:23:44,140
it was just blood, sweat and tears.

305
00:23:44,141 --> 00:23:49,480
Leon Moysheef created the two-level Manhattan suspension bridge.

306
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:54,260
While it looks light because of its color and delicate suspension cables,

307
00:23:54,261 --> 00:23:58,580
its strength can be measured in almost 100 years of service.

308
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:03,600
North of the Williamsburg Bridge,

309
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:07,560
arching the East River and crossing Roosevelt Island,

310
00:24:08,660 --> 00:24:11,220
